  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/NASCETPercentStenosis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/Measurement"/>
    <rdfs:label>NASCET percent stenosis</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Percentage reduction of the internal carotid lumen, by the NASCET method.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>MS-000014</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>Measurement</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:quantityKind>fraction</cde:quantityKind>
    <cde:permittedUnit>%</cde:permittedUnit>
    <cde:measurementMethod>Residual lumen at the stenosis divided by the diameter of the normal distal internal carotid artery, beyond the bulb. The denominator is the landmark that makes this method carotid-specific.</cde:measurementMethod>
    <cde:designNote>Separate from the ECST method rather than a value on one measurement, because they are different numbers from the same image: roughly 70 percent NASCET is 85 percent ECST. A model that lets a consumer read one as the other is worse than one carrying neither.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>proposed</cde:versionStatus>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:created>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:lastModified>
  </rdf:Description>
