    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/237495005"/>
    <cde:designNote>Margin values follow ACR TI-RADS 2017: smooth, ill-defined, lobulated or irregular, extra-thyroidal extension. Lobulated and irregular are one scoring category in the scheme and are kept separate here, because a radiologist can say which and the scheme discarding that is the scheme's choice, not ours. Spiculated is subsumed under irregular, which TI-RADS defines as jagged, spiculated or sharp angles.</cde:designNote>
