  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/LungCancer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/Diagnosis"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nd8a51b0774744059a648016dace851b9"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N03c1d97eb32b4253995fd41a715ee411"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N36501fcd7aa444e080e479a58c9ac569"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N21e74c7152194a7e81e7897190bb0aa9"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N8477604930174bcb9cd00957c32f5397"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nb2b8af44e2514307a98606e6834bc829"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N6dfd4dd42e1a4d379fe48c3bba23b9d2"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N08b1b9c38dc043c99630bab7957c17c3"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nd3551d08b8dd4c1a9b3a319ef06236d8"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N4f29b45f58444dbf89ef3becad216f84"/>
    <rdfs:label>lung cancer</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>lung cancer</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>Primary malignant neoplasm arising from lung tissue.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>DX-000004</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>Diagnosis</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-LungCancer-RADLEX-RID45686"/>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-LungCancer-SNOMEDCT-363358000"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://www.radlex.org/RID/RID45686"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/363358000"/>
    <cde:hasSynonym rdf:nodeID="Ndf5b46dde806425baa6462aea35b17ff"/>
    <skos:altLabel>bronchogenic carcinoma</skos:altLabel>
    <cde:designNote>Points at each attenuation subtype separately rather than at the parent. Singling out one subtype while the rest relied on the parent edge implied that solid and non-solid nodules were not suggestive of cancer, and left part-solid carrying two specificities at once, one inherited and one direct. NEEDS A RADIOLOGIST: the three specificity values. The claim as written is that part-solid is the most specific for malignancy, solid the commonest presentation but least specific because most solid nodules are benign, and non-solid occasional and indolent. It also reaches a finding by two different edges in different roles: it manifests as a nodule and it causes an effusion.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>proposed</cde:versionStatus>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:created>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:lastModified>
  </rdf:Description>
