  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/HeartFailure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/Diagnosis"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N8a9c0f646aa149468b88d427e8bf15dc"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nfceb6760d5374c14a181545b1b08e9d2"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N5bc180c676804bed98b9f68b4d625883"/>
    <rdfs:label>heart failure</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>heart failure</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>Inability of the heart to maintain adequate output, with venous congestion.</skos:definition>
    <cde:localId>DX-000015</cde:localId>
    <cde:nodeType>Diagnosis</cde:nodeType>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-HeartFailure-RADLEX-RID34795"/>
    <cde:hasBinding rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/binding-HeartFailure-SNOMEDCT-84114007"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://www.radlex.org/RID/RID34795"/>
    <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://snomed.info/id/84114007"/>
    <cde:designNote>Causes the oedema rather than manifesting as it: heart failure raises left atrial pressure and fluid accumulates, which is production of a second entity. Nothing here shows itself as anything, which is why it has no manifestation edge at all. Carried as a node so causal edges have a target; it has no imaging elements of its own and is not something a radiologist reports seeing.</cde:designNote>
    <cde:noImagingElements rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</cde:noImagingElements>
    <cde:versionNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1</cde:versionNumber>
    <cde:versionStatus>proposed</cde:versionStatus>
    <cde:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:created>
    <cde:lastModified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-09-14</cde:lastModified>
  </rdf:Description>
